      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a true crisis, the assertive Mediterranean temperament is often more immediately effective because they are less likely to get bogged down in lengthy group consensus. Over-indexing on the consensus model can indeed lead to decision paralysis when rapid, decisive action is required to mitigate immediate danger. Therefore, for high-intensity crisis management, the directness of the Mediterranean style often provides a statistically faster path to resolution.",
